Faculty are expected to engage in ongoing professional development and, as appropriate to the appointment, scholarly achievement, continued preparation and study, student growth and development, and service to the university and community.   Department of Nursing Science: https://www.stcloudstate.edu/nursing/ Inter Faculty Organization collective bargaining agreement: https://www.ifo.org/ Position Overview   The Department of Nursing Science offers a pre-licensure Bachelor of Science in Nursing program and a fully online RN-BS Completion Program. The pre-licensure program is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) and approved by the Minnesota Board of Nursing. Educational and clinical experiences prepare graduates to provide person-centered nursing care in diverse and rapidly changing health care environments.   The department emphasizes clinical judgment, evidence-based practice, quality and safety, interprofessional collaboration, population health, professional identity, and preparation for the NCLEX-RN. Students learn through classroom, clinical, simulation, laboratory, and technology-enhanced experiences, supported by the Jim and Ann Marie Maciej Nursing Education Suite and strong regional clinical partnerships.   Primary Responsibilities   • Teach undergraduate nursing courses in classroom, clinical, simulation, and/or online environments, with a primary anticipated focus in general acute care nursing.   • Support student learning, clinical judgment development, professional formation, and progression toward entry-level nursing practice.   • Provide academic advising, mentoring, and guidance to undergraduate nursing students.   • Collaborate with nursing faculty, staff, adjunct clinical faculty, preceptors, and community/clinical partners.   • Participate in curriculum development, program evaluation, assessment of student learning, and continuous quality improvement.   • Contribute to accreditation, regulatory, governance, and departmental service activities.   • Engage in professional development, scholarly or creative activity, and service consistent with the expectations of a probationary faculty appointment and the IFO collective bargaining agreement.   • Participate in departmental initiatives related to contemporary nursing education, including simulation, clinical judgment, the AACN Essentials, NCLEX-RN, and Next Generation NCLEX (NGN), as appropriate .     Appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank will be determined based on the successful candidate’s education, academic and professional experience, scholarly accomplishments, and qualifications consistent with St. Cloud State University and Minnesota State policies and the applicable collective bargaining agreement     Why Join SCSU Nursing?   This position offers an opportunity to help educate the next generation of nurses while building an academic career within a collaborative department. Faculty benefit from strong relationships with regional health care and community partners, opportunities to teach across multiple learning environments, and meaningful engagement in curriculum innovation, simulation, clinical judgment, student mentoring, and professional service. The department especially welcomes experienced clinicians who are interested in bringing their practice expertise into nursing education.     Salary Range: *The salary range denoted is the contractual range; however, salary upon hire is dependent upon qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution completed by the date of appointment.   Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license in the United States and eligibility for Minnesota RN licensure by the date of appointment.   Minimum of two years of professional nursing practice experience.   Clinical knowledge or professional experience relevant to general acute care nursing and/or a related area of nursing practice.   Demonstrated potential for effective teaching, clinical instruction, precepting, mentoring, staff development, or professional nursing education.   Effective oral, written, interpersonal, and collaborative communication skills.   Demonstrated ability to work effectively with students, colleagues, clinical partners, and individuals from diverse backgrounds.   Commitment to student success and preparation of nurses for contemporary professional practice.   Preferred Qualification  Doctoral degree in nursing or a related field (PhD, DNP, EdD), completed or in progress.   Graduate preparation, certification, or substantial clinical expertise in adult acute care, medical-surgical, critical care, emergency, progressive care, perioperative, or other related acute care nursing practice.   Teaching experience in a baccalaureate nursing program or other higher-education setting .   Experience teaching in clinical, simulation, skills laboratory, online, hybrid, or technology-enhanced learning environments.   Experience mentoring or precepting nursing students, new graduate nurses, or practicing nurses.   Familiarity with contemporary nursing education frameworks and standards, including the AACN Essentials, clinical judgment, NCLEX-RN, and Next Generation NCLEX (NGN).   Evidence of scholarly activity or demonstrated potential for scholarship appropriate to the faculty role.   Experience with curriculum development, program assessment, accreditation, regulatory review, or academic service.   Demonstrated interest in continued professional development and advancement as a nurse educator.   Documents Needed to Apply Current curriculum vitae or resume.   Cover letter addressing the minimum qualifications and describing the applicant’s interest in the position, relevant nursing practice experience, teaching/mentoring experience or potential, and general acute care or related specialty expertise .   Contact information for three professional references who can address the applicant’s clinical 